✅ Advantages
Pipeline configuration lives in source control.
Changes can be reviewed through pull requests.
Easy to track changes and roll back configuration.
Templates help standardize workflows across projects.
Supports scalable CI/CD and multi-stage pipelines.
Enables pipeline configuration to evolve alongside application code.
❌ Disadvantages
Requires familiarity with YAML syntax and indentation.
Complex pipelines can be difficult to read without good structure.
Incorrect conditions, permissions, or configuration can break a pipeline.
Some Classic features and configuration patterns require different YAML implementations.
